# NOTE (Render): Render's documented way to configure redirects/rewrites for a Static Site is
# the Dashboard (Static Site -> Redirects/Rewrites tab), NOT a _redirects file in the repo —
# unlike Netlify/Cloudflare Pages. If the rules below aren't taking effect live, add the same
# 3 rules there (Source / Destination / Action), in this order. This file is kept so the intent
# is documented in version control and in case Render's static-site runtime does pick it up.
#
# 1) Canonicalize /index.html -> / (avoids duplicate-content: same page reachable at 2 URLs)
#    Source: /index.html   Destination: /   Action: Redirect
/index.html   /   301

# 2) Proxy SEO files so Google always sees them on this domain, content comes live from backend
#    Source: /sitemap.xml  Destination: https://digitalbazaar-backend-1qdt.onrender.com/sitemap.xml  Action: Rewrite
#    Source: /robots.txt   Destination: https://digitalbazaar-backend-1qdt.onrender.com/robots.txt   Action: Rewrite
/sitemap.xml  https://digitalbazaar-backend-1qdt.onrender.com/sitemap.xml  200
/robots.txt   https://digitalbazaar-backend-1qdt.onrender.com/robots.txt   200
